// http.tls_cert's key loading (tls.X509KeyPair) on the native backends
// (std/native/llrt/tlssrv.xo, the zero-C audit's B31) against Go's: RSA
// keys as PKCS #1 and PKCS #8, P-256 and P-384 keys as SEC 1 and PKCS #8,
// an Ed25519 key as PKCS #8, then the errors (another key of the same
// type, a key of another type, an X25519 key, a key that does not
// parse); then an HTTPS request to a server with each good RSA and ECDSA
// pair, the client trusting that certificate. Test keys only, generated once by a
// scratch Go program.
